From 0ab3227c2c266bbb875bfe6c3c83e47d1d7caa99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:41:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 38/58] dns: the TCP, TLS and HTTPS transports under loss

A pipelined TCP or TLS connection carries a bounded number of queries; DNS over HTTPS resets its
transport on a timeout only when no later query was answered, asks again when the server closes
without a GOAWAY, and compares the starts of queries by the monotonic clock.

Made of these commits of the earlier series (branch archive/r25-1.14-commits):
  70eed8cd6 dns/transport: cap queries in flight on a pipelined TCP/TLS connection
  4a02b27eb dns/https: reset the transport on a timeout only when no later query was answered
  362e7748e dns/https: ask a query again when the server closes the connection without a GOAWAY
  25f2d213d dns/https: compare the starts of queries by the monotonic clock

Pdk-Feature: dns-transport
Pdk-Zone: core
Pdk-Layer: 04
